#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""jev-no-bullshit: a Stop hook for Claude Code and Codex, and the check behind the pi and opencode plugins.

When a turn ends, ask Jev (TypeSafe's System One model) whether the model's
final summary bullshits about what it did, measured against the tool calls it
actually made. If Jev flags a type of bullshit, send the model back with
feedback on that type. See docs/jev-no-bullshit-spec.md.

Standard library only. Reads TYPESAFE_API_KEY from the environment, or else
from ~/.config/jev-no-bullshit/env. Always exits 0 and fails open: any error
lets the turn end, with a systemMessage saying the reply was not checked.

Claude Code and Codex send a Stop event naming their transcript. The pi and
opencode plugins (pi/, opencode/) have no transcript file to name, so they send
the turn itself: {"host", "session_id", "task", "actions", "earlier_actions",
"conversation", "model", "last_assistant_message", "stop_hook_active"}, each
action being {"tool", "input", "result", "error"} and each conversation message
{"role", "text"}, oldest first, ending before the reply.
"""

